// EXPECT: E0233 — an array length that is not an integer literal (ADR-0039 §3a)
// `jr-sema` has no constant evaluator: ADR-0018 §3 puts const-eval in `jr-db` over the
// bytecode VM, which is *downstream* of where a type annotation is resolved. So the
// length is read during lowering and only a literal is accepted. `[COUNT]u8` becomes
// possible in the wave that makes sema and comptime mutually recursive (W4).
COUNT :: 4;

main :: () {
    buf: [COUNT]u8;
}
